<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Seven Interpretive Essays on Peruvian Reality</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1928</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Siete ensayos de interpretación de la realidad peruana</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Seven Interpretive Essays on Peruvian Reality (Siete ensayos de interpretación de la realidad peruana) is a book by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-carlos-mariategui">José Carlos Mariátegui</a> published in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lima">Lima</a> in 1928. Applying Marxist analysis to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>, it treated the condition of the indigenous population as a problem of land and examined the economy, education, religion, regionalism and literature. It became one of the most influential works of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> American social thought.</p></div>
